      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm leaning towards AWS Secrets Manager for this task, primarily because of its popularity and managed nature. I need to make sure to create `fetch_db_secret.py`, but it seems a good managed service is the best way forward.\n\n\n**Implementing Secret Retrieval**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS Secrets Manager, as it aligns well with the brief. I'm focusing on the implementation now, and will use the `boto3` library. The plan is to create a `fetch_db_secret` function that handles the secret retrieval, taking the secret name as input and returning the secret string. The code will include provider-specific identifiers.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819905570,
          "start": 1789819903664
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9945eb00017rNy0xR4Rg9o6r",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9945964001rEmv1IrK4Dosv7",
      "session_id": "ses_f466ba6aeffeOAbTE8MZXejBor",
      "time_created": 1789819903664,
